Description: borderless GNOME Console with a compact tab strip
 Removes the GNOME Console (kgx) title bar and replaces its header bar with a slim
 tab strip, without patching Console itself.
 .
 Console builds its window from a GtkBuilder template compiled into its binary as
 /org/gnome/Console/kgx-window.ui. G_RESOURCE_OVERLAYS can replace that single
 resource, so no patch to Console is required - the overlay is dropped in at launch.
 .
 The package installs the launcher, the checker tools and the stylesheet, but
 installs nothing into any user account and enables nothing. Run
 .
   kgx-compact-install
 .
 as your own user, then follow the gsettings command it prints.
 .
 This is deliberate: G_RESOURCE_OVERLAYS and the GTK4 user stylesheet are both
 per-user, and the generated overlay is pinned to the Console version installed on
 that machine, so a global enable would be wrong.
Homepage: https://github.com/tongtf/kgx-compact